{
  "video": {
    "id": "YnF1b_Kqf88",
    "title": "Agarose Gel Electrophoresis, DNA Sequencing, PCR, Excerpt 1 | MIT 7.01SC Fundamentals of Biology",
    "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YnF1b_Kqf88",
    "channel": "MIT OpenCourseWare",
    "duration": 1067,
    "language": "en"
  },
  "segment_count": 295,
  "segments": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "start": 6.31,
      "end": 8.18,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "So far, there are a lot of ways to clone genes."
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "start": 8.18,
      "end": 9.24,
      "duration": 1.06,
      "text": "I've given you two."
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "start": 9.24,
      "end": 12.06,
      "duration": 2.82,
      "text": "Later in the course, I'll give you a third, but we cloned it"
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "start": 12.06,
      "end": 13.87,
      "duration": 1.81,
      "text": "here by its function, complementation."
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "start": 13.87,
      "end": 15.35,
      "duration": 1.48,
      "text": "We cloned it here on the basis of the"
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "start": 15.35,
      "end": 17.275,
      "duration": 1.925,
      "text": "protein it actually made."
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "start": 17.275,
      "end": 19.58,
      "duration": 2.305,
      "text": "Now, how do we analyze these genes?"
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "start": 19.58,
      "end": 21.27,
      "duration": 1.69,
      "text": "How do you know which gene we're dealing with?"
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "start": 21.27,
      "end": 22.63,
      "duration": 1.36,
      "text": "How do we study it?"
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "start": 22.63,
      "end": 23.85,
      "duration": 1.22,
      "text": "Let's turn to that."
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "start": 23.85,
      "end": 25.136,
      "duration": 1.286,
      "text": "Analyzing our gene."
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "start": 32.29,
      "end": 35.57,
      "duration": 3.28,
      "text": "Well, let's suppose we have our cell, maybe"
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "start": 35.57,
      "end": 36.3,
      "duration": 0.73,
      "text": "it's our yeast cell."
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "start": 36.3,
      "end": 37.17,
      "duration": 0.87,
      "text": "It's Arg1 again."
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "start": 37.17,
      "end": 40.26,
      "duration": 3.09,
      "text": "We'll go back to yeast."
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "start": 40.26,
      "end": 44.24,
      "duration": 3.98,
      "text": "It's got its yeast DNA it's also got this circle that has"
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "start": 44.24,
      "end": 46.26,
      "duration": 2.02,
      "text": "our plasmid here."
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "start": 46.26,
      "end": 48.25,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "Circle is plasmid."
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "start": 48.25,
      "end": 50.02,
      "duration": 1.77,
      "text": "How are we going to study that gene?"
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "start": 50.02,
      "end": 52.35,
      "duration": 2.33,
      "text": "We know that yeast is able to now grow."
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "start": 52.35,
      "end": 53.75,
      "duration": 1.4,
      "text": "We can grow up that yeast."
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "start": 53.75,
      "end": 56.42,
      "duration": 2.67,
      "text": "We can purify DNA from it."
    },
    {
      "index": 22,
      "start": 56.42,
      "end": 56.67,
      "duration": 0.25,
      "text": "But wait a second."
    },
    {
      "index": 23,
      "start": 56.67,
      "end": 59.07,
      "duration": 2.4,
      "text": "How do we get our plasmids away from the chromosomal DNA?"
    },
    {
      "index": 24,
      "start": 59.07,
      "end": 61.07,
      "duration": 2.0,
      "text": "Aren't we back in the same boat of you can't"
    },
    {
      "index": 25,
      "start": 61.07,
      "end": 62.33,
      "duration": 1.26,
      "text": "purify DNA from DNA?"
    },
    {
      "index": 26,
      "start": 66.4,
      "end": 68.12,
      "duration": 1.72,
      "text": "Thankfully, this is easy."
    },
    {
      "index": 27,
      "start": 68.12,
      "end": 71.21,
      "duration": 3.09,
      "text": "Little circles of DNA have different biochemical"
    },
    {
      "index": 28,
      "start": 71.21,
      "end": 73.78,
      "duration": 2.57,
      "text": "properties than the long, linear chromosomes or the big"
    },
    {
      "index": 29,
      "start": 73.78,
      "end": 75.11,
      "duration": 1.33,
      "text": "chunks of DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 30,
      "start": 75.11,
      "end": 77.76,
      "duration": 2.65,
      "text": "And you can use biochemistry to separate little circles of"
    },
    {
      "index": 31,
      "start": 77.76,
      "end": 80.83,
      "duration": 3.07,
      "text": "DNA from big chunks of DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 32,
      "start": 80.83,
      "end": 82.08,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "So no problem."
    },
    {
      "index": 33,
      "start": 82.08,
      "end": 84.36,
      "duration": 2.28,
      "text": "You can purify the plasmids."
    },
    {
      "index": 34,
      "start": 84.36,
      "end": 90.82,
      "duration": 6.46,
      "text": "Purify the plasmid, and there it is."
    },
    {
      "index": 35,
      "start": 90.82,
      "end": 92.1,
      "duration": 1.28,
      "text": "It's back again."
    },
    {
      "index": 36,
      "start": 92.1,
      "end": 95.23,
      "duration": 3.13,
      "text": "And now, you've got your Arg1 gene."
    },
    {
      "index": 37,
      "start": 95.23,
      "end": 97.436,
      "duration": 2.206,
      "text": "How do I study it?"
    },
    {
      "index": 38,
      "start": 97.436,
      "end": 100.23,
      "duration": 2.794,
      "text": "Well, the first thing I might want to find out about my Arg1"
    },
    {
      "index": 39,
      "start": 100.23,
      "end": 104.83,
      "duration": 4.6,
      "text": "gene, is how big is that insert."
    },
    {
      "index": 40,
      "start": 104.83,
      "end": 107.445,
      "duration": 2.615,
      "text": "How can I find out how big that insert is?"
    },
    {
      "index": 41,
      "start": 107.445,
      "end": 108.355,
      "duration": 0.91,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: Electrophoresis."
    },
    {
      "index": 42,
      "start": 108.355,
      "end": 110.16,
      "duration": 1.805,
      "text": "ERIC LANDER: Electrophoresis."
    },
    {
      "index": 43,
      "start": 110.16,
      "end": 111.61,
      "duration": 1.45,
      "text": "I first have to cut out the insert."
    },
    {
      "index": 44,
      "start": 111.61,
      "end": 112.816,
      "duration": 1.206,
      "text": "How do I do that?"
    },
    {
      "index": 45,
      "start": 112.816,
      "end": 114.184,
      "duration": 1.368,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: The restriction enzyme."
    },
    {
      "index": 46,
      "start": 114.184,
      "end": 116.64,
      "duration": 2.456,
      "text": "ERIC LANDER: My restriction enzyme, EcoRI."
    },
    {
      "index": 47,
      "start": 116.64,
      "end": 120.86,
      "duration": 4.22,
      "text": "I cut with EcoRI and it liberates the insert."
    },
    {
      "index": 48,
      "start": 120.86,
      "end": 128.28,
      "duration": 7.42,
      "text": "And then I take a gel, which can be made out of different"
    },
    {
      "index": 49,
      "start": 128.28,
      "end": 130.47,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "substances, and I put my DNA there."
    },
    {
      "index": 50,
      "start": 130.47,
      "end": 133.51,
      "duration": 3.04,
      "text": "Agarose is particularly nice stuff, which is basically"
    },
    {
      "index": 51,
      "start": 133.51,
      "end": 137.98,
      "duration": 4.47,
      "text": "Jell-O. And I turn on an electric field."
    },
    {
      "index": 52,
      "start": 137.98,
      "end": 140.26,
      "duration": 2.28,
      "text": "DNA is what, positively charged or negatively charged?"
    },
    {
      "index": 53,
      "start": 140.26,
      "end": 141.18,
      "duration": 0.92,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: Negative."
    },
    {
      "index": 54,
      "start": 141.18,
      "end": 143.3,
      "duration": 2.12,
      "text": "ERIC LANDER: So what kind of charge do I want to put here?"
    },
    {
      "index": 55,
      "start": 143.3,
      "end": 144.29,
      "duration": 0.99,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: Positive."
    },
    {
      "index": 56,
      "start": 144.29,
      "end": 145.55,
      "duration": 1.26,
      "text": "ERIC LANDER: What charge do I put here?"
    },
    {
      "index": 57,
      "start": 145.55,
      "end": 146.265,
      "duration": 0.715,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: Negative."
    },
    {
      "index": 58,
      "start": 146.265,
      "end": 148.78,
      "duration": 2.515,
      "text": "ERIC LANDER: What happens if I do it backwards?"
    },
    {
      "index": 59,
      "start": 148.78,
      "end": 149.59,
      "duration": 0.81,
      "text": "Bad."
    },
    {
      "index": 60,
      "start": 149.59,
      "end": 152.09,
      "duration": 2.5,
      "text": "Everybody does it backwards in the lab at some point."
    },
    {
      "index": 61,
      "start": 152.09,
      "end": 154.95,
      "duration": 2.86,
      "text": "So then you do this."
    },
    {
      "index": 62,
      "start": 154.95,
      "end": 159.22,
      "duration": 4.27,
      "text": "The DNA goes this way and it turns out that agarose is this"
    },
    {
      "index": 63,
      "start": 159.22,
      "end": 161.7,
      "duration": 2.48,
      "text": "matrix of cross links and all that."
    },
    {
      "index": 64,
      "start": 161.7,
      "end": 166.66,
      "duration": 4.96,
      "text": "And DNA molecules wiggle through like a snake, through"
    },
    {
      "index": 65,
      "start": 166.66,
      "end": 170.43,
      "duration": 3.77,
      "text": "this matrix, and little ones go much faster than big ones."
    },
    {
      "index": 66,
      "start": 170.43,
      "end": 176.93,
      "duration": 6.5,
      "text": "So what happens is, little DNA molecules move faster than big"
    },
    {
      "index": 67,
      "start": 176.93,
      "end": 178.66,
      "duration": 1.73,
      "text": "DNA molecules."
    },
    {
      "index": 68,
      "start": 178.66,
      "end": 182.52,
      "duration": 3.86,
      "text": "And if I stop at some point, and I add a dye that sticks to"
    },
    {
      "index": 69,
      "start": 182.52,
      "end": 185.85,
      "duration": 3.33,
      "text": "DNA, and look at it with a fluorescent light, I can"
    },
    {
      "index": 70,
      "start": 185.85,
      "end": 188.52,
      "duration": 2.67,
      "text": "actually see where the DNA molecules are."
    },
    {
      "index": 71,
      "start": 188.52,
      "end": 191.85,
      "duration": 3.33,
      "text": "So I've grown up a ton of this plasmid, lots of it, couple of"
    },
    {
      "index": 72,
      "start": 191.85,
      "end": 193.05,
      "duration": 1.2,
      "text": "micrograms of it."
    },
    {
      "index": 73,
      "start": 193.05,
      "end": 196.26,
      "duration": 3.21,
      "text": "I cut it, I add it to the top of my well here, I turn on the"
    },
    {
      "index": 74,
      "start": 196.26,
      "end": 200.33,
      "duration": 4.07,
      "text": "electricity, and it wiggle, wiggle, wiggles through."
    },
    {
      "index": 75,
      "start": 200.33,
      "end": 206.18,
      "duration": 5.85,
      "text": "This is the vector, and this is the insert."
    },
    {
      "index": 76,
      "start": 206.18,
      "end": 209.01,
      "duration": 2.83,
      "text": "It might be actually, that I found another plasmid that"
    },
    {
      "index": 77,
      "start": 209.01,
      "end": 211.18,
      "duration": 2.17,
      "text": "could do this too, that rescued yeast."
    },
    {
      "index": 78,
      "start": 211.18,
      "end": 213.87,
      "duration": 2.69,
      "text": "It had a vector and maybe at a different insert."
    },
    {
      "index": 79,
      "start": 213.87,
      "end": 216.455,
      "duration": 2.585,
      "text": "Maybe I had one, I don't know why, that had the same insert"
    },
    {
      "index": 80,
      "start": 216.455,
      "end": 217.49,
      "duration": 1.035,
      "text": "right there."
    },
    {
      "index": 81,
      "start": 217.49,
      "end": 219.81,
      "duration": 2.32,
      "text": "In any case, the first characterization that I would"
    },
    {
      "index": 82,
      "start": 219.81,
      "end": 223.47,
      "duration": 3.66,
      "text": "do is look at the size of my insert."
    },
    {
      "index": 83,
      "start": 223.47,
      "end": 226.01,
      "duration": 2.54,
      "text": "How big is that insert?"
    },
    {
      "index": 84,
      "start": 226.01,
      "end": 239.45,
      "duration": 13.44,
      "text": "I might find out that the insert is one kilobase, 1,000"
    },
    {
      "index": 85,
      "start": 239.45,
      "end": 246.74,
      "duration": 7.29,
      "text": "bases, or one KB, or 2 KB or something like that."
    },
    {
      "index": 86,
      "start": 246.74,
      "end": 248.975,
      "duration": 2.235,
      "text": "That's a first order of characterization."
    },
    {
      "index": 87,
      "start": 248.975,
      "end": 250.58,
      "duration": 1.605,
      "text": "Now, of course, what I really want to know"
    },
    {
      "index": 88,
      "start": 250.58,
      "end": 253.95,
      "duration": 3.37,
      "text": "about the insert, sequence."
    },
    {
      "index": 89,
      "start": 253.95,
      "end": 255.91,
      "duration": 1.96,
      "text": "I want the DNA sequencing insert, right?"
    },
    {
      "index": 90,
      "start": 255.91,
      "end": 258.05,
      "duration": 2.14,
      "text": "Let's not just mess around with, it's got 1,000 bases, I"
    },
    {
      "index": 91,
      "start": 258.05,
      "end": 260.11,
      "duration": 2.06,
      "text": "want to know what are those bases in what order."
    },
    {
      "index": 92,
      "start": 260.11,
      "end": 262.32,
      "duration": 2.21,
      "text": "So that means I have to invent DNA sequencing."
    },
    {
      "index": 93,
      "start": 273.06,
      "end": 273.79,
      "duration": 0.73,
      "text": "All right."
    },
    {
      "index": 94,
      "start": 273.79,
      "end": 276.35,
      "duration": 2.56,
      "text": "So how am I going to invent DNA sequencing?"
    },
    {
      "index": 95,
      "start": 276.35,
      "end": 278.55,
      "duration": 2.2,
      "text": "This is a little tough."
    },
    {
      "index": 96,
      "start": 278.55,
      "end": 280.265,
      "duration": 1.715,
      "text": "I have my piece of DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 97,
      "start": 280.265,
      "end": 282.28,
      "duration": 2.015,
      "text": "I cut it out."
    },
    {
      "index": 98,
      "start": 282.28,
      "end": 288.772,
      "duration": 6.492,
      "text": "Here's my piece of DNA, 5 prime to 3 prime,"
    },
    {
      "index": 99,
      "start": 288.772,
      "end": 290.09,
      "duration": 1.318,
      "text": "5 prime to 3 prime."
    },
    {
      "index": 100,
      "start": 292.9,
      "end": 303.33,
      "duration": 10.43,
      "text": "Let's give it a sequence ATTAAGAATGCAT, et cetera."
    },
    {
      "index": 101,
      "start": 307.37,
      "end": 311.62,
      "duration": 4.25,
      "text": "DNA sequencing is actually remarkably cute."
    },
    {
      "index": 102,
      "start": 311.62,
      "end": 316.37,
      "duration": 4.75,
      "text": "I take a primer just like Kornberg did back when he was"
    },
    {
      "index": 103,
      "start": 316.37,
      "end": 318.88,
      "duration": 2.51,
      "text": "discovering polymerase."
    },
    {
      "index": 104,
      "start": 318.88,
      "end": 321.45,
      "duration": 2.57,
      "text": "Here's my primer, let's say."
    },
    {
      "index": 105,
      "start": 321.45,
      "end": 322.7,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "Here's my primer."
    },
    {
      "index": 106,
      "start": 325.73,
      "end": 326.98,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "Here's the matching template."
    },
    {
      "index": 107,
      "start": 330.79,
      "end": 332.66,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "And what did Kornberg teaches us?"
    },
    {
      "index": 108,
      "start": 332.66,
      "end": 335.11,
      "duration": 2.45,
      "text": "He taught us that if we add polymerase, what will"
    },
    {
      "index": 109,
      "start": 335.11,
      "end": 338.04,
      "duration": 2.93,
      "text": "polymerase do?"
    },
    {
      "index": 110,
      "start": 338.04,
      "end": 339.91,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "It'll add the right bases, right?"
    },
    {
      "index": 111,
      "start": 339.91,
      "end": 346.91,
      "duration": 7.0,
      "text": "TACGTA onward."
    },
    {
      "index": 112,
      "start": 346.91,
      "end": 348.85,
      "duration": 1.94,
      "text": "If we could look really fast, maybe we could just"
    },
    {
      "index": 113,
      "start": 348.85,
      "end": 351.19,
      "duration": 2.34,
      "text": "see it going by."
    },
    {
      "index": 114,
      "start": 351.19,
      "end": 353.39,
      "duration": 2.2,
      "text": "But we can't look really fast."
    },
    {
      "index": 115,
      "start": 353.39,
      "end": 359.11,
      "duration": 5.72,
      "text": "If we just add polymerase, it'll just zip up"
    },
    {
      "index": 116,
      "start": 359.11,
      "end": 360.67,
      "duration": 1.56,
      "text": "and add all the bases."
    },
    {
      "index": 117,
      "start": 363.5,
      "end": 366.59,
      "duration": 3.09,
      "text": "But someone had a clever trick."
    },
    {
      "index": 118,
      "start": 366.59,
      "end": 368.66,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "The clever trick is this."
    },
    {
      "index": 119,
      "start": 368.66,
      "end": 376.86,
      "duration": 8.2,
      "text": "Suppose I threw in a smidgen of defective Ts, Ts that"
    },
    {
      "index": 120,
      "start": 376.86,
      "end": 378.55,
      "duration": 1.69,
      "text": "couldn't be extended for some reason?"
    },
    {
      "index": 121,
      "start": 381.06,
      "end": 382.31,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "I'll call that T star."
    },
    {
      "index": 122,
      "start": 388.48,
      "end": 390.64,
      "duration": 2.16,
      "text": "What happens if a defective T goes in there?"
    },
    {
      "index": 123,
      "start": 393.7,
      "end": 394.95,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "Can't be extended anymore."
    },
    {
      "index": 124,
      "start": 398.43,
      "end": 399.93,
      "duration": 1.5,
      "text": "And what happens then to my reaction?"
    },
    {
      "index": 125,
      "start": 399.93,
      "end": 401.18,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "It comes to a halt."
    },
    {
      "index": 126,
      "start": 403.56,
      "end": 407.52,
      "duration": 3.96,
      "text": "Ah, but what happened if I put in a good T?"
    },
    {
      "index": 127,
      "start": 407.52,
      "end": 415.232,
      "duration": 7.712,
      "text": "Then instead, what would the next base be?"
    },
    {
      "index": 128,
      "start": 415.232,
      "end": 419.78,
      "duration": 4.548,
      "text": "A. Then what would happen?"
    },
    {
      "index": 129,
      "start": 419.78,
      "end": 425.47,
      "duration": 5.69,
      "text": "C, G. Then what's next?"
    },
    {
      "index": 130,
      "start": 425.47,
      "end": 430.46,
      "duration": 4.99,
      "text": "T. And what would happen if I put in a defective T?"
    },
    {
      "index": 131,
      "start": 434.52,
      "end": 435.77,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "It would stop."
    },
    {
      "index": 132,
      "start": 445.33,
      "end": 449.34,
      "duration": 4.01,
      "text": "Now, maybe instead the defective T didn't go in."
    },
    {
      "index": 133,
      "start": 455.86,
      "end": 459.22,
      "duration": 3.36,
      "text": "And it would go on, and the next T that it encounters,"
    },
    {
      "index": 134,
      "start": 459.22,
      "end": 462.48,
      "duration": 3.26,
      "text": "maybe it would put a defective T there."
    },
    {
      "index": 135,
      "start": 462.48,
      "end": 466.75,
      "duration": 4.27,
      "text": "Or maybe it would put a defective T there."
    },
    {
      "index": 136,
      "start": 469.83,
      "end": 471.52,
      "duration": 1.69,
      "text": "Now, of course, I just have a little smidgen of"
    },
    {
      "index": 137,
      "start": 471.52,
      "end": 474.02,
      "duration": 2.5,
      "text": "defective T, right?"
    },
    {
      "index": 138,
      "start": 474.02,
      "end": 475.65,
      "duration": 1.63,
      "text": "So which of these will happen?"
    },
    {
      "index": 139,
      "start": 475.65,
      "end": 478.92,
      "duration": 3.27,
      "text": "Will it sometimes stop at the first T?"
    },
    {
      "index": 140,
      "start": 478.92,
      "end": 481.16,
      "duration": 2.24,
      "text": "Sometimes at the second?"
    },
    {
      "index": 141,
      "start": 481.16,
      "end": 482.41,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "Sometimes at the third?"
    },
    {
      "index": 142,
      "start": 485.19,
      "end": 488.26,
      "duration": 3.07,
      "text": "I'll actually get a series of molecules."
    },
    {
      "index": 143,
      "start": 488.26,
      "end": 492.35,
      "duration": 4.09,
      "text": "What will the lengths of those molecules tell me?"
    },
    {
      "index": 144,
      "start": 492.35,
      "end": 493.82,
      "duration": 1.47,
      "text": "Where the Ts are."
    },
    {
      "index": 145,
      "start": 497.96,
      "end": 499.71,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "Kind of cute."
    },
    {
      "index": 146,
      "start": 499.71,
      "end": 501.89,
      "duration": 2.18,
      "text": "This is very cute."
    },
    {
      "index": 147,
      "start": 501.89,
      "end": 509.34,
      "duration": 7.45,
      "text": "So if I do that reaction, I'll call that the defective Ts, I"
    },
    {
      "index": 148,
      "start": 509.34,
      "end": 513.26,
      "duration": 3.92,
      "text": "could see that there is some molecules, stop here at this"
    },
    {
      "index": 149,
      "start": 513.26,
      "end": 516.15,
      "duration": 2.89,
      "text": "very small size, some stop here, some stop here, some"
    },
    {
      "index": 150,
      "start": 516.15,
      "end": 517.89,
      "duration": 1.74,
      "text": "stop there, some stop there."
    },
    {
      "index": 151,
      "start": 517.89,
      "end": 520.01,
      "duration": 2.12,
      "text": "And what have I just learned?"
    },
    {
      "index": 152,
      "start": 520.01,
      "end": 523.95,
      "duration": 3.94,
      "text": "The sizes, the lengths of the fragments that end in T."
    },
    {
      "index": 153,
      "start": 523.95,
      "end": 524.7,
      "duration": 0.75,
      "text": "But that's not good."
    },
    {
      "index": 154,
      "start": 524.7,
      "end": 527.352,
      "duration": 2.652,
      "text": "I also want to know the As."
    },
    {
      "index": 155,
      "start": 527.352,
      "end": 529.09,
      "duration": 1.738,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: Do it with defective As."
    },
    {
      "index": 156,
      "start": 529.09,
      "end": 530.91,
      "duration": 1.82,
      "text": "ERIC LANDER: Do it will defective As, right?"
    },
    {
      "index": 157,
      "start": 530.91,
      "end": 534.18,
      "duration": 3.27,
      "text": "I'll just use defective As."
    },
    {
      "index": 158,
      "start": 534.18,
      "end": 538.52,
      "duration": 4.34,
      "text": "And then I'll see the As stop there."
    },
    {
      "index": 159,
      "start": 538.52,
      "end": 540.54,
      "duration": 2.02,
      "text": "And then I'll do it with defective Cs, and I'll do it"
    },
    {
      "index": 160,
      "start": 540.54,
      "end": 542.54,
      "duration": 2.0,
      "text": "with defective Gs."
    },
    {
      "index": 161,
      "start": 542.54,
      "end": 546.57,
      "duration": 4.03,
      "text": "And I'll see exactly where the molecules are, the lengths of"
    },
    {
      "index": 162,
      "start": 546.57,
      "end": 554.09,
      "duration": 7.52,
      "text": "the molecules that end in A, T, C, and G."
    },
    {
      "index": 163,
      "start": 554.09,
      "end": 557.62,
      "duration": 3.53,
      "text": "And I've just read the sequence, haven't I?"
    },
    {
      "index": 164,
      "start": 557.62,
      "end": 559.18,
      "duration": 1.56,
      "text": "Pretty cool."
    },
    {
      "index": 165,
      "start": 559.18,
      "end": 561.01,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "This actually is so cool, it won a Nobel Prize."
    },
    {
      "index": 166,
      "start": 563.73,
      "end": 566.152,
      "duration": 2.422,
      "text": "I mean cool usually means won a Nobel Prize or something"
    },
    {
      "index": 167,
      "start": 566.152,
      "end": 567.98,
      "duration": 1.828,
      "text": "like that in this class."
    },
    {
      "index": 168,
      "start": 567.98,
      "end": 570.3,
      "duration": 2.32,
      "text": "So actually, how do I visualize the"
    },
    {
      "index": 169,
      "start": 570.3,
      "end": 572.52,
      "duration": 2.22,
      "text": "little letters there?"
    },
    {
      "index": 170,
      "start": 572.52,
      "end": 575.78,
      "duration": 3.26,
      "text": "So the little fragments on the gel?"
    },
    {
      "index": 171,
      "start": 575.78,
      "end": 577.48,
      "duration": 1.7,
      "text": "I visualize the little fragments back in"
    },
    {
      "index": 172,
      "start": 577.48,
      "end": 579.076,
      "duration": 1.596,
      "text": "ancient days, yes?"
    },
    {
      "index": 173,
      "start": 579.076,
      "end": 581.992,
      "duration": 2.916,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: How do you know [INAUDIBLE]"
    },
    {
      "index": 174,
      "start": 585.394,
      "end": 587.518,
      "duration": 2.124,
      "text": "necessarily be inserted in every place"
    },
    {
      "index": 175,
      "start": 587.518,
      "end": 588.768,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "where there is a letter?"
    },
    {
      "index": 176,
      "start": 590.74,
      "end": 592.5,
      "duration": 1.76,
      "text": "ERIC LANDER: I'd make the right ratio."
    },
    {
      "index": 177,
      "start": 592.5,
      "end": 595.29,
      "duration": 2.79,
      "text": "I'd choose a ratio of defective to good Ts."
    },
    {
      "index": 178,
      "start": 595.29,
      "end": 598.51,
      "duration": 3.22,
      "text": "Like if I choose 1% defective T's, then about 1% of the"
    },
    {
      "index": 179,
      "start": 598.51,
      "end": 600.92,
      "duration": 2.41,
      "text": "time, I put in the defective T it turns out."
    },
    {
      "index": 180,
      "start": 600.92,
      "end": 602.56,
      "duration": 1.64,
      "text": "It turns out to work OK."
    },
    {
      "index": 181,
      "start": 602.56,
      "end": 606.02,
      "duration": 3.46,
      "text": "I just put in a smidgen of defective Ts, like 1%, and 1%"
    },
    {
      "index": 182,
      "start": 606.02,
      "end": 609.26,
      "duration": 3.24,
      "text": "of the time it stops here, and 1% here, and 1% there."
    },
    {
      "index": 183,
      "start": 609.26,
      "end": 613.67,
      "duration": 4.41,
      "text": "So and then, of course, to see them in old days, what people"
    },
    {
      "index": 184,
      "start": 613.67,
      "end": 617.54,
      "duration": 3.87,
      "text": "did was they made these primers radioactive, and these"
    },
    {
      "index": 185,
      "start": 617.54,
      "end": 622.05,
      "duration": 4.51,
      "text": "radioactive primers here within the gel would be held"
    },
    {
      "index": 186,
      "start": 622.05,
      "end": 625.38,
      "duration": 3.33,
      "text": "up against a piece of x-ray film, and you would see where"
    },
    {
      "index": 187,
      "start": 625.38,
      "end": 627.66,
      "duration": 2.28,
      "text": "little radioactive bands were."
    },
    {
      "index": 188,
      "start": 627.66,
      "end": 629.69,
      "duration": 2.03,
      "text": "That's how you could visualize the primers, because it turns"
    },
    {
      "index": 189,
      "start": 629.69,
      "end": 631.46,
      "duration": 1.77,
      "text": "out you have too little primer to see it even with my"
    },
    {
      "index": 190,
      "start": 631.46,
      "end": 632.62,
      "duration": 1.16,
      "text": "fluorescent dye."
    },
    {
      "index": 191,
      "start": 632.62,
      "end": 636.43,
      "duration": 3.81,
      "text": "But a little radioactivity, you add radioactivity, you"
    },
    {
      "index": 192,
      "start": 636.43,
      "end": 639.48,
      "duration": 3.05,
      "text": "take the gel off, you put on a piece of, I guess you've got"
    },
    {
      "index": 193,
      "start": 639.48,
      "end": 640.69,
      "duration": 1.21,
      "text": "to wrap it with Saran."
    },
    {
      "index": 194,
      "start": 640.69,
      "end": 642.045,
      "duration": 1.355,
      "text": "You'd better be standing behind a shield."
    },
    {
      "index": 195,
      "start": 642.045,
      "end": 644.06,
      "duration": 2.015,
      "text": "So you're standing behind a plastic shield, you reach"
    },
    {
      "index": 196,
      "start": 644.06,
      "end": 646.51,
      "duration": 2.45,
      "text": "around the shield, you wrap it with Saran Wrap."
    },
    {
      "index": 197,
      "start": 646.51,
      "end": 648.34,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "You then put x-ray film on."
    },
    {
      "index": 198,
      "start": 648.34,
      "end": 649.76,
      "duration": 1.42,
      "text": "You are you doing this in a dark room."
    },
    {
      "index": 199,
      "start": 649.76,
      "end": 650.98,
      "duration": 1.22,
      "text": "You then seal it up."
    },
    {
      "index": 200,
      "start": 650.98,
      "end": 652.6,
      "duration": 1.62,
      "text": "You put it in the freezer for two weeks."
    },
    {
      "index": 201,
      "start": 652.6,
      "end": 653.21,
      "duration": 0.61,
      "text": "You take it out."
    },
    {
      "index": 202,
      "start": 653.21,
      "end": 654.05,
      "duration": 0.84,
      "text": "You develop it."
    },
    {
      "index": 203,
      "start": 654.05,
      "end": 656.38,
      "duration": 2.33,
      "text": "You get your magic marker, and you follow where all the"
    },
    {
      "index": 204,
      "start": 656.38,
      "end": 658.16,
      "duration": 1.78,
      "text": "little bands are."
    },
    {
      "index": 205,
      "start": 658.16,
      "end": 659.41,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "And that's DNA sequencing."
    },
    {
      "index": 206,
      "start": 663.3,
      "end": 663.66,
      "duration": 0.36,
      "text": "It's cool."
    },
    {
      "index": 207,
      "start": 663.66,
      "end": 664.355,
      "duration": 0.695,
      "text": "It won a Nobel Prize."
    },
    {
      "index": 208,
      "start": 664.355,
      "end": 667.16,
      "duration": 2.805,
      "text": "It's also like really tedious."
    },
    {
      "index": 209,
      "start": 667.16,
      "end": 673.49,
      "duration": 6.33,
      "text": "So little tricks were done to speed it up, some nice pieces"
    },
    {
      "index": 210,
      "start": 673.49,
      "end": 675.91,
      "duration": 2.42,
      "text": "of engineering."
    },
    {
      "index": 211,
      "start": 675.91,
      "end": 690.62,
      "duration": 14.71,
      "text": "Instead of visualizing our DNA, faster DNA sequencing,"
    },
    {
      "index": 212,
      "start": 690.62,
      "end": 691.87,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "what happens instead?"
    },
    {
      "index": 213,
      "start": 695.27,
      "end": 698.64,
      "duration": 3.37,
      "text": "What people did, which was very cool, was they simply"
    },
    {
      "index": 214,
      "start": 698.64,
      "end": 703.39,
      "duration": 4.75,
      "text": "took the As, Ts, Cs and Gs, the defective ones, they"
    },
    {
      "index": 215,
      "start": 703.39,
      "end": 707.15,
      "duration": 3.76,
      "text": "attached a colored dye to each one."
    },
    {
      "index": 216,
      "start": 707.15,
      "end": 711.81,
      "duration": 4.66,
      "text": "The As were green, and the Ts were blue and the Gs were red."
    },
    {
      "index": 217,
      "start": 711.81,
      "end": 716.9,
      "duration": 5.09,
      "text": "Now, when I run it out, I can do it with fluorescence."
    },
    {
      "index": 218,
      "start": 716.9,
      "end": 720.9,
      "duration": 4.0,
      "text": "And I can see the Ts all glow one color, and the As glow"
    },
    {
      "index": 219,
      "start": 720.9,
      "end": 722.75,
      "duration": 1.85,
      "text": "another color."
    },
    {
      "index": 220,
      "start": 722.75,
      "end": 726.34,
      "duration": 3.59,
      "text": "Now, it turns out, of course, if they're glowing four"
    },
    {
      "index": 221,
      "start": 726.34,
      "end": 730.09,
      "duration": 3.75,
      "text": "different colors, I don't actually need to run them in"
    },
    {
      "index": 222,
      "start": 730.09,
      "end": 732.33,
      "duration": 2.24,
      "text": "separate lanes."
    },
    {
      "index": 223,
      "start": 732.33,
      "end": 734.78,
      "duration": 2.45,
      "text": "I could run them in the same lane, right?"
    },
    {
      "index": 224,
      "start": 734.78,
      "end": 749.95,
      "duration": 15.17,
      "text": "So I could run them all in a single lane, and I'd see Ts"
    },
    {
      "index": 225,
      "start": 749.95,
      "end": 753.753,
      "duration": 3.803,
      "text": "and As, and Gs."
    },
    {
      "index": 226,
      "start": 757.56,
      "end": 763.5,
      "duration": 5.94,
      "text": "And now, instead of putting this up against the piece of"
    },
    {
      "index": 227,
      "start": 763.5,
      "end": 765.8,
      "duration": 2.3,
      "text": "x-ray film, I could do this in a very thin"
    },
    {
      "index": 228,
      "start": 765.8,
      "end": 767.05,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "tube called a capillary."
    },
    {
      "index": 229,
      "start": 773.81,
      "end": 777.96,
      "duration": 4.15,
      "text": "And instead of holding it up to an x-ray film, I could just"
    },
    {
      "index": 230,
      "start": 777.96,
      "end": 779.21,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "put a laser detector."
    },
    {
      "index": 231,
      "start": 783.17,
      "end": 786.975,
      "duration": 3.805,
      "text": "I can turn on the electricity and watch the fragments go by"
    },
    {
      "index": 232,
      "start": 786.975,
      "end": 789.2,
      "duration": 2.225,
      "text": "and just look at it with my laser detector."
    },
    {
      "index": 233,
      "start": 789.2,
      "end": 789.89,
      "duration": 0.69,
      "text": "Shines a light."
    },
    {
      "index": 234,
      "start": 789.89,
      "end": 792.9,
      "duration": 3.01,
      "text": "I say, oh yeah, green, red, blue."
    },
    {
      "index": 235,
      "start": 792.9,
      "end": 795.44,
      "duration": 2.54,
      "text": "That's the sequence."
    },
    {
      "index": 236,
      "start": 795.44,
      "end": 798.02,
      "duration": 2.58,
      "text": "This made it a lot easier than that."
    },
    {
      "index": 237,
      "start": 798.02,
      "end": 800.07,
      "duration": 2.05,
      "text": "I actually got involved in molecular biology when it was"
    },
    {
      "index": 238,
      "start": 800.07,
      "end": 802.68,
      "duration": 2.61,
      "text": "still that."
    },
    {
      "index": 239,
      "start": 802.68,
      "end": 804.12,
      "duration": 1.44,
      "text": "That is a lot better."
    },
    {
      "index": 240,
      "start": 809.54,
      "end": 811.75,
      "duration": 2.21,
      "text": "By the way, I didn't tell you what the defective"
    },
    {
      "index": 241,
      "start": 811.75,
      "end": 813.148,
      "duration": 1.398,
      "text": "Ts were, did I?"
    },
    {
      "index": 242,
      "start": 813.148,
      "end": 816.284,
      "duration": 3.136,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: [INAUDIBLE]."
    },
    {
      "index": 243,
      "start": 816.284,
      "end": 817.23,
      "duration": 0.946,
      "text": "ERIC LANDER: Sorry?"
    },
    {
      "index": 244,
      "start": 817.23,
      "end": 818.565,
      "duration": 1.335,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: [INAUDIBLE]."
    },
    {
      "index": 245,
      "start": 818.565,
      "end": 820.49,
      "duration": 1.925,
      "text": "ERIC LANDER: Well, they gotta have something that prevents"
    },
    {
      "index": 246,
      "start": 820.49,
      "end": 823.38,
      "duration": 2.89,
      "text": "them from being extended, right?"
    },
    {
      "index": 247,
      "start": 823.38,
      "end": 824.92,
      "duration": 1.54,
      "text": "What prevents them from being extended?"
    },
    {
      "index": 248,
      "start": 824.92,
      "end": 830.71,
      "duration": 5.79,
      "text": "Do we remember how DNA is extended?"
    },
    {
      "index": 249,
      "start": 830.71,
      "end": 833.39,
      "duration": 2.68,
      "text": "We have a sugar phosphate backbone, right?"
    },
    {
      "index": 250,
      "start": 833.39,
      "end": 844.85,
      "duration": 11.46,
      "text": "Phosphate, base, 5 prime."
    },
    {
      "index": 251,
      "start": 844.85,
      "end": 847.35,
      "duration": 2.5,
      "text": "Where do we extend, what base?"
    },
    {
      "index": 252,
      "start": 847.35,
      "end": 848.3,
      "duration": 0.95,
      "text": "3 prime."
    },
    {
      "index": 253,
      "start": 848.3,
      "end": 851.4,
      "duration": 3.1,
      "text": "And what do we use to extend on?"
    },
    {
      "index": 254,
      "start": 851.4,
      "end": 853.67,
      "duration": 2.27,
      "text": "The 3 prime hydroxyl."
    },
    {
      "index": 255,
      "start": 853.67,
      "end": 856.97,
      "duration": 3.3,
      "text": "Remember, DNA has no hydroxyl at its 2 prime position."
    },
    {
      "index": 256,
      "start": 856.97,
      "end": 864.22,
      "duration": 7.25,
      "text": "Its normal DNA is 2 prime deoxy."
    },
    {
      "index": 257,
      "start": 867.65,
      "end": 870.536,
      "duration": 2.886,
      "text": "How do you think we prevent it from being extended?"
    },
    {
      "index": 258,
      "start": 870.536,
      "end": 872.41,
      "duration": 1.874,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: 2 prime [INAUDIBLE]."
    },
    {
      "index": 259,
      "start": 872.41,
      "end": 874.16,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "ERIC LANDER: 2 prime, 3 prime dideoxy."
    },
    {
      "index": 260,
      "start": 877.23,
      "end": 884.7,
      "duration": 7.47,
      "text": "Defective just means 2 prime, 3 prime dideoxy."
    },
    {
      "index": 261,
      "start": 887.22,
      "end": 889.14,
      "duration": 1.92,
      "text": "See, we tell you about these structure not just so you"
    },
    {
      "index": 262,
      "start": 889.14,
      "end": 891.43,
      "duration": 2.29,
      "text": "memorize structures, but because those are the tricks"
    },
    {
      "index": 263,
      "start": 891.43,
      "end": 892.58,
      "duration": 1.15,
      "text": "we use in the trade."
    },
    {
      "index": 264,
      "start": 892.58,
      "end": 901.26,
      "duration": 8.68,
      "text": "Now, you get yourself some 2 prime, 3 prime dideoxies."
    },
    {
      "index": 265,
      "start": 901.26,
      "end": 903.69,
      "duration": 2.43,
      "text": "You put in a smidgen, maybe 1%."
    },
    {
      "index": 266,
      "start": 903.69,
      "end": 905.02,
      "duration": 1.33,
      "text": "You run your reaction."
    },
    {
      "index": 267,
      "start": 905.02,
      "end": 909.12,
      "duration": 4.1,
      "text": "Those dideoxies have dyes, spelled differently, D-Y-E"
    },
    {
      "index": 268,
      "start": 909.12,
      "end": 911.25,
      "duration": 2.13,
      "text": "color dyes attached to them."
    },
    {
      "index": 269,
      "start": 911.25,
      "end": 914.19,
      "duration": 2.94,
      "text": "And you sit there with your laser detector."
    },
    {
      "index": 270,
      "start": 914.19,
      "end": 916.27,
      "duration": 2.08,
      "text": "Turns out to be even better."
    },
    {
      "index": 271,
      "start": 916.27,
      "end": 920.27,
      "duration": 4.0,
      "text": "If you have one capillary, you could have two."
    },
    {
      "index": 272,
      "start": 920.27,
      "end": 922.67,
      "duration": 2.4,
      "text": "If you have two, you could have three, and the machines"
    },
    {
      "index": 273,
      "start": 922.67,
      "end": 931.285,
      "duration": 8.615,
      "text": "that were built around 1999 had 96 capillaries."
    },
    {
      "index": 274,
      "start": 934.59,
      "end": 937.62,
      "duration": 3.03,
      "text": "I'll call it 100."
    },
    {
      "index": 275,
      "start": 937.62,
      "end": 945.06,
      "duration": 7.44,
      "text": "You could sit there and read 700 bases every hour."
    },
    {
      "index": 276,
      "start": 948.48,
      "end": 951.64,
      "duration": 3.16,
      "text": "You can do this maybe 20 hours in the day"
    },
    {
      "index": 277,
      "start": 951.64,
      "end": 952.89,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "because it's automated."
    },
    {
      "index": 278,
      "start": 955.29,
      "end": 959.892,
      "duration": 4.602,
      "text": "You could do this 360 days a year."
    },
    {
      "index": 279,
      "start": 959.892,
      "end": 966.53,
      "duration": 6.638,
      "text": "And at MIT, we had 100 machines during the Human"
    },
    {
      "index": 280,
      "start": 966.53,
      "end": 967.71,
      "duration": 1.18,
      "text": "Genome Project."
    },
    {
      "index": 281,
      "start": 967.71,
      "end": 976.98,
      "duration": 9.27,
      "text": "And if you do the arithmetic, we could read about 60 billion"
    },
    {
      "index": 282,
      "start": 976.98,
      "end": 987.61,
      "duration": 10.63,
      "text": "bases a year, 60 billion bases a year during the height of"
    },
    {
      "index": 283,
      "start": 987.61,
      "end": 988.86,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "the Human Genome Project."
    },
    {
      "index": 284,
      "start": 995.9,
      "end": 1012.65,
      "duration": 16.75,
      "text": "Now, this is pretty cool, but it ain't nothing compared to"
    },
    {
      "index": 285,
      "start": 1012.65,
      "end": 1016.49,
      "duration": 3.84,
      "text": "what we're doing 10 years later."
    },
    {
      "index": 286,
      "start": 1016.49,
      "end": 1032.25,
      "duration": 15.76,
      "text": "Currently, we are doing 60 billion bases every"
    },
    {
      "index": 287,
      "start": 1032.25,
      "end": 1037.039,
      "duration": 4.789,
      "text": "10 minutes at MIT."
    },
    {
      "index": 288,
      "start": 1040.819,
      "end": 1045.01,
      "duration": 4.191,
      "text": "There's a little trick that I'll tell you about next time"
    },
    {
      "index": 289,
      "start": 1045.01,
      "end": 1049.5,
      "duration": 4.49,
      "text": "of how DNA sequencing went from that, where you could do"
    },
    {
      "index": 290,
      "start": 1049.5,
      "end": 1054.11,
      "duration": 4.61,
      "text": "about 250 letters a day, when I first got involved in this,"
    },
    {
      "index": 291,
      "start": 1054.11,
      "end": 1057.42,
      "duration": 3.31,
      "text": "to that, where at a large facility like MIT, you could"
    },
    {
      "index": 292,
      "start": 1057.42,
      "end": 1061.33,
      "duration": 3.91,
      "text": "do 60 billion letters a day, to today when you can do about"
    },
    {
      "index": 293,
      "start": 1061.33,
      "end": 1063.75,
      "duration": 2.42,
      "text": "60 billion letters in 10 minutes."
    },
    {
      "index": 294,
      "start": 1063.75,
      "end": 1065.03,
      "duration": 1.28,
      "text": "We'll touch on that next time."
    }
  ],
